ABSTRACT

This project presents the design, development, and deployment of an
Anomaly Detection Platform — a machine learning system that
simultaneously addresses two high-impact real-world domains:
financial fraud detection and network intrusion detection. The platform
integrates modular ML pipelines, dual-layer detection combining
supervised XGBoost models with unsupervised Isolation Forest
anomaly scoring, SHAP-based explainability, a REST API backend
built on FastAPI, and an interactive Streamlit dashboard deployed live
on Streamlit Cloud.
The updated fraud detection module is based on the IEEE-CIS Fraud
Detection dataset. The pipeline automatically loads transaction and
identity data, joins records on TransactionID, handles missing values,
encodes categorical fields, scales numerical features, and trains
XGBoost with class imbalance handled through scale_pos_weight. A
200,000-row IEEE-CIS training run achieved an XGBoost ROC-AUC of
0.9411 and an average precision score of 0.6796. The combined
XGBoost and Isolation Forest risk score achieved ROC-AUC of 0.9373.
The intrusion detection module uses the NSL-KDD dataset and
evaluates Random Forest and XGBoost classifiers, with XGBoost
achieving ROC-AUC of 0.9696. The system is served through FastAPI

and demonstrated through a Streamlit dashboard that supports single-
record prediction and CSV-based batch prediction.

Keywords: Anomaly Detection, IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection, NSL-KDD,
XGBoost, Isolation Forest, SHAP Explainability, FastAPI, Streamlit,
Machine Learning Deployment.

